---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Colleen Shifflett"
  description="Ten years of analytics across financial services, SaaS, media, and government. I work on the layer of your website most teams never think about."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>There's the back end, the front end, and then there's my end.</h1>

        <p>
          My end is information design, content design, and experiment design:
          how your site is organized, what it says, and how you learn what's
          working. It's a layer most people never think about. I bring it into
          view. That's what the name means, too. A bright cave is a hidden space
          with the light turned on.
        </p>

        <h2>The art, science, and math of web strategy</h2>
        <p>
          The art is the words, structure, and labels that help people see
          themselves on your site. The science is the method: small changes,
          honest feedback, and learning what works. The math is the measurement:
          data accurate enough to make decisions, without chasing perfection.
        </p>

        <h2>Where I come from</h2>
        <p>
          I've spent ten years in analytics across financial services, B2B SaaS,
          media, and federal government. I was a founding member of the UX data
          analysis team at IRS Online Services, and I've trained more than 500
          non-technical professionals to use their own data with confidence.
          Today I also work as an embedded analytics engineer, which keeps the
          math side of my practice sharp.
        </p>

        <h2>What I've learned</h2>
        <p>
          Right-sized beats sophisticated. The best web program is the one your
          team can actually run.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
